    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d238">

                <pb facs="0394" n="300" xml:id="pg300"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Sir
                            Julian Pauncefote.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-03-27"><hi rendition="#italic">March 27,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 356.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: Referring to previous correspondence
                    concerning the claim of James Bain against the United States, I have the honor
                    to inform you that the case was referred to the Committee on Foreign Affairs of
                    the House of Representatives on the 27th ultimo, with a favorable recommendation
                    from this Department, and the additional facts contained in your note of the 23d
                    instant have to-day been communicated to the committee.</p>
                <p>As soon as the determination of the committee is known it will be communicated to
                    you.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
